  "final_message": "I'm stopping before I change anything, because removing `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event conflicts with ARCH-4.\n\n`channel` is part of the published `OrderPlaced` payload (`src/core/events.ts:16` and `:50`). CLAUDE.md says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume that event from other repositories, and that no change may break a deployed consumer. Changes have to be additive, and removals go through deprecation. I can't see those repos, so I can't confirm that nothing reads the field. Removing it outright could break a deployed consumer without any failure showing up here.\n\nThere's a second, smaller problem. `POST /orders` currently requires `channel` and returns 400 without it. Dropping the field from the order model would change that contract for callers too. The same applies to the stored order shape, which is used by `GET /orders/{id}` (ARCH-8, web-storefront).\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Deprecate first (my suggestion).** Mark `channel` as deprecated in the event and model and make it optional on input. Keep emitting it on `OrderPlaced`. Remove it later, once billing-service and analytics-ingest owners confirm they don't read it.\n2. **Remove only the internal parts now.** Drop `channel` from validation and the input contract (optional and ignored), and keep it in the event and the order response until the consumers are confirmed.\n3. **Full removal.** If you've already confirmed with both consumer teams that nothing reads it, tell me and I'll remove it everywhere. That covers the event, the model, parsing, validation, tests and the docs examples.\n\nWhich one do you want?",
